---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const entry = await getEntry("home", "page");
if (!entry) {
  throw new Error("Missing home page content");
}

const email = entry.data.footer.email;
const meta = {
  title: "Terms of Service | Marres",
  description:
    "Read the terms that govern accounts, subscriptions, submitted data, outputs, payments, and use of the Marres service.",
  canonicalUrl: "https://marres.io/terms",
};
---

<SiteLayout {...meta}>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-content">
      <span class="tag">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Effective 3 September 2026</p>
      <p class="legal-intro">
        These terms govern your use of Marres, a service provided by Marres
        Insights Pte Ltd. By creating an account or using the service, you agree
        to these terms.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Accounts and access</h2>
        <p>
          You must give accurate account information, keep your credentials
          secure, and use only the company tenant that you are authorised to
          use. You are responsible for activity under your account unless you
          tell us promptly about unauthorised access.
        </p>
        <p>
          Access to paid analysis depends on the subscription and entitlement
          state confirmed through Stripe. We may suspend access when payment
          fails, a subscription ends, these terms are breached, or continued
          access creates a security or legal risk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Subscriptions and payment</h2>
        <p>
          The price and billing period shown during Stripe checkout apply to
          your purchase. Stripe provides the hosted checkout and billing pages.
          An account owner can open Stripe's billing portal from Marres and use
          the options available there.
        </p>
        <p>
          A checkout success page does not grant access by itself. Marres grants
          paid access only after it confirms the paid billing state. Mandatory
          rights under applicable law still apply.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Permitted use</h2>
        <p>
          Use Marres only for lawful internal business purposes. Do not use the
          service to violate another person's rights, interfere with the
          service, bypass access controls, submit malicious content, or obtain
          data that you are not authorised to use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your data and responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for the company names, Google Maps URLs,
          competitor choices, domain selections, and other material you submit.
          You must have the right to submit and use that material. You must not
          submit credentials, payment-card details, or private personal data
          that the service does not request.
        </p>
        <p>
          You retain your rights in submitted material. You grant Marres a
          non-exclusive licence to process it only as needed to provide, secure,
          support, and improve the reliability of the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Marres outputs and intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Marres and its licensors retain rights in the service, software,
          methods, designs, and general know-how. While your account has the
          required access, you may use outputs produced for your tenant inside
          your business. You may not resell the service or its outputs, remove
          source notices, or present an output as independent professional
          advice without written permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Marres uses third-party services for public review collection, model
          processing, hosting, and billing. Their systems and terms can affect
          availability. Marres remains responsible for its own service boundary,
          but it does not control third-party services or public source content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Decision-support limits</h2>
        <p>
          Marres provides informational business decision support. Outputs are
          based on available public reviews, selected comparison data, and model
          processing. They can be incomplete, wrong, or outdated. They do not
          guarantee an outcome and are not legal, financial, tax, medical, or
          other professional advice. You remain responsible for decisions and
          actions taken from an output.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Availability and warranties</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to operate Marres with reasonable care, but we do not promise
          uninterrupted access, error-free output, complete source coverage, or
          a specific business result. To the extent permitted by law, the
          service is provided as available and without implied warranties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, Marres Insights Pte Ltd is not liable
          for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential loss, lost profit,
          lost revenue, lost opportunity, or loss caused by a decision made from
          an output. Its total liability arising from the service is limited to
          the amount you paid for Marres in the 12 months before the event that
          caused the claim.
        </p>
        <p>
          This limit does not apply where liability cannot legally be limited,
          including liability for fraud or wilful misconduct.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Ending use</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using Marres at any time. Subscription changes take
          effect according to the billing state returned by Stripe. Terms that
          must continue by their nature, including payment, intellectual
          property, liability, and governing-law terms, remain in effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law and contact</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of Singapore. The courts of
          Singapore have exclusive jurisdiction over disputes arising from these
          terms or the service.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contact <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with a question about these
          terms.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
